---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/visitors.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Visitors | Economic Machine Learning Lab">
    <section class="banner">
        <div class="banner-content">
            <h1>Visitors</h1>
            <p>Visits and exchanges with industry, government, and academic institutions</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <div class="container visitors-layout">
        <main>
            <section class="visitors-intro">
                <h2>Visits to EML</h2>
                <p>EML welcomes visitors from industry, government, and academic institutions to exchange perspectives and discuss research collaborations. This page records upcoming and past visits.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="visitors-section" aria-labelledby="upcoming-visits">
                <h2 id="upcoming-visits">Upcoming Visits</h2>
                <article class="visitor-card" id="kpx-2026">
                    <p class="visitor-date">November 13, 2026</p>
                    <h3><a href="https://www.kpx.or.kr/eng/">Korea Power Exchange (KPX)</a> — South Korea</h3>
                    <p class="visitor-names">Minwoo Jang and Yongsik Kim</p>
                    <p class="visitor-team">Supply and Demand Forecasting Team, Energy Planning Department</p>
                    <p>KPX operates South Korea's electricity market and power system and plays a central role in national electricity supply-and-demand planning.</p>
                    <p>Representatives from KPX will visit the EML Lab at Indiana University to discuss electricity demand forecasting, particularly the challenges of predicting large new electricity loads and managing long-term uncertainty. KPX initiated the visit to seek EML's perspectives on forecasting methodologies, data requirements, and ongoing research.</p>
                    <p>EML Research Director Joon Y. Park and his research collaborators in Korea, including EML collaborator <a href="https://econ.cau.ac.kr/en/portfolio-items/choi-yongok/">Yongok Choi</a>, have developed core electricity-demand forecasting models for KPX for more than 30 years. This longstanding relationship provides a foundation for continued research exchange and collaboration.</p>
                </article>
            </section>
        </main>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
